Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||11-26-2000||01:25 PM||||well heres the story- my brother, dad, and I have been working on restoring an old vw bug for some time now, and recently got it working. with the current engine, the car is somewhat of a torque pig, but not much on the horsepower. my brother, being a new driver, is alwaqys out trying to get races with the bug, and recently, got whupped by a friend of his, with an 86 honda civic. well, after much deliberation, we decided to see who's car actually has USABLE power, and chained the 2 cars back to back, in a literal DRAG race. well, all in all, the honda smoked its tires while the bug pulled him around backwards. BTW, both these cars a crapwagons, so dont worry about any potential damage. the only shortcoming with the bug was that it overheated (came close, we have temp gagues on every cylinder. i know that i post the wierdest stories on the forum (probably?) but its just the wierd stuff I do. oh yeah, i whupped a new trans am (in the rain) guy hit the rev limiter in first because he tried to launch hard. love that weight over the wheels man.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||11-26-2000||01:39 PM||||So, were people asking you, "What're you trying to pull?"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Guess the bug comes out ahead of the civic, when you compare the two back-to-back, eh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">?<P>Man, that felt good to get that out of my system...my apologies.    ||||reg||12
Z||000002||Wolfhound||11-26-2000||04:09 PM||||FieroStetz, Does the number three cylinder run hotter on the VDub?<P>If you drop a valve it always seems to be the number three cylinder. I have messed with VW's for years. Just curious!||||reg||5
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||11-26-2000||06:05 PM||||Sounds like you had fun.  I kinda did the same thing when i was in high school.  except in involved an old toyota corolla and a k5 blazer.  needless to say that blazer won.  it was up on 38's and had a full blown 350.  the corolla didnt have a driver.  we chained it up. took it back to our muddin hole at the time.  then tried to see how many times we could roll it.  cant really remember how many times it rolled(you usually dont do stuff like this when your sober)  but the next day the car looked like it was put in a trash compacter.  pretty fun.  i miss high school.....<BR>joejoe||||reg||1
Z||000004||robertjay||11-26-2000||06:10 PM||||The forward most left side cylinder runs hotter than the rest on a bug because of the oil cooler just above it.  The cooling air being blown over that cylinder is slightly preheated.  I bought one that had a hole in the crown of the piston.  I was expecting all of them to have similar damage, but that was the only one.||||reg||1
